{"term":"chunk","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0fec65b720ca4238ae","definition":"A part of something that has been separated; a generally squat, thick, irregular piece of something, e.g. wood or stone.","example":"The statue broke into chunks.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bit","hunk","lump","bit","chip","chunk","tranche","clip","crumb","crumbling","cutting","flake","fleak","fragment","hunk","lump","mammock","ort","piece","piecemeal","portion","scrap","scraplet","slice","snead","snippet","steck"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chunk-blower","chunkful","chunkification","chunkify","chunklength","chunkless","chunklet","chunklike","chunk of change","chunkserver","chunkster","chunkwise","chunky","kerchunk","subchunk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5148da3a3c093dd8a9","definition":"A sequence of two or more words that occur in language with high frequency but are not idiomatic.","example":"In fact, some linguists suggest that 45 percent to 60 percent of what you produce in your L1 is functional chunks of language. These chunks of language also give you some sense of fluency.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bundle","cluster"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chunk-blower","chunkful","chunkification","chunkify","chunklength","chunkless","chunklet","chunklike","chunk of change","chunkserver","chunkster","chunkwise","chunky","kerchunk","subchunk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fdfe6b5bfff383a36f","definition":"A discrete segment of a file, stream, etc. (especially one that represents audiovisual media); a block.","example":"The first DWORD of a chunk data in the RIFF chunk is a four character code value identifying the form type of the file.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chunk-blower","chunkful","chunkification","chunkify","chunklength","chunkless","chunklet","chunklike","chunk of change","chunkserver","chunkster","chunkwise","chunky","kerchunk","subchunk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29eb02c6bdf121574e","definition":"A segment of a comedian's performance.","example":"You begin gathering two hours of dependable comedy by developing that first three-minute chunk. When you're satisfied with it, you create another three minutes of laughs, then another three minutes.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chunk-blower","chunkful","chunkification","chunkify","chunklength","chunkless","chunklet","chunklike","chunk of change","chunkserver","chunkster","chunkwise","chunky","kerchunk","subchunk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25fcce06319168a550","definition":"To break into large pieces or chunks.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["chunk-blower","chunkful","chunkification","chunkify","chunklength","chunkless","chunklet","chunklike","chunk of change","chunkserver","chunkster","chunkwise","chunky","kerchunk","subchunk","chunkable","chunker","dechunk","microchunk","mischunk","prechunk","rechunk"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chunk#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5257b146d6f63a9f40","definition":"To break down (